>I'm a novice player (almost always die before level 5 novice)

How do you die? We may need to talk about some pacifist techniques that
may help you. Many novice Nethack players believe that best way to
get through the early game is to kill everything in sight and to ramp up
on levels and HP. The opposite can often be a better technique.

Take a read of the pacifist FAQ here:

http://home.nycap.rr.com/rduhan/steves/pacfaq02.html

You may find that incorporating some of these techniques will get you
further into the game.


> and I
>have a lot of problems managing my inventory at the beginning of the
>game.  I tend to get burdened because I'm carrying around a lot of
>stuff that I haven't had the chance to identify yet.

That's simple. Don't carry it. As long as it's un-IDed, it isn't very useful
to you.

>  Two questions: 1) what items should I leave behind initially,

Anything that you are not actively using.

> and 2) what's a safe way to
>leave things behind so that other creatures won't take them?

Boxes/chests are the best. 

